<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S3.SS3" title="In 3. Empirical Analysis ‣ Systems-Level Attack Surface of Edge Agent Deployments on IoT" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">3.3 </span>Data Sovereignty and Egress</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1" title="In 3.3. Data Sovereignty and Egress ‣ 3. Empirical Analysis ‣ Systems-Level Attack Surface of Edge Agent Deployments on IoT" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Forced fallback: sovereignty under stress.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S3.SS4" title="In 3. Empirical Analysis ‣ Systems-Level Attack Surface of Edge Agent Deployments on IoT" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">3.4 </span>Failover Vulnerability Windows</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S3.SS4.SSS0.Px1" title="In 3.4. Failover Vulnerability Windows ‣ 3. Empirical Analysis ‣ Systems-Level Attack Surface of Edge Agent Deployments on IoT" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Method.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S3.SS4.SSS0.Px2" title="In 3.4. Failover Vulnerability Windows ‣ 3. Empirical Analysis ‣ Systems-Level Attack Surface of Edge Agent Deployments on IoT" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">End-to-end failover.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S3.SS4.SSS0.Px3" title="In 3.4. Failover Vulnerability Windows ‣ 3. Empirical Analysis ‣ Systems-Level Attack Surface of Edge Agent Deployments on IoT" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">MQTT reconnection in isolation (<math class="ltx_Math" alttext="N{=}50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N{=}50</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S3.SS4.SSS0.Px4" title="In 3.4. Failover Vulnerability Windows ‣ 3. Empirical Analysis ‣ Systems-Level Attack Surface of Edge Agent Deployments on IoT" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Implication.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section"><a href="#S4" title="In Systems-Level Attack Surface of Edge Agent Deployments on IoT" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">4 </span>Discussion</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_section">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S4.SS1" title="In 4. Discussion ‣ Systems-Level Attack Surface of Edge Agent Deployments on IoT" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">4.1 </span>Architecture IS Security Posture</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S4.SS2" title="In 4. Discussion ‣ Systems-Level Attack Surface of Edge Agent Deployments on IoT" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">4.2 </span>The Provenance Gap</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S4.SS3" title="In 4. Discussion ‣ Systems-Level Attack Surface of Edge Agent Deployments on IoT" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">4.3 </span>Emergent Coordination Failures</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1" title="In 4.3. Emergent Coordination Failures ‣ 4. Discussion ‣ Systems-Level Attack Surface of Edge Agent Deployments on IoT" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">State-plane divergence (S1b).</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2" title="In 4.3. Emergent Coordination Failures ‣ 4. Discussion ‣ Systems-Level Attack Surface of Edge Agent Deployments on IoT" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Induced trust erosion (S1c).</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
